The review found four defects and two latency problems in the last delivery; all are fixed and re-verified. Nothing you asked for was missing, but (a) and (b) were each wrong in specific situations and the decode-stage prefetch never ran. The host API is unchanged apart from a new, optional JoinTactic::prefetch.

Defects

(b) fired while switched off. After set_params with abandon_pct < 0, resting orders stayed armed and the ratio test passed, so an order reaching the front was cancelled as abandoned.
(b) counted round lots that no longer were. Flags were only ever added, so a market order flagged for one of our orders and later cut below a round lot still counted for our next one. Against a per-order model this gave a false (b) in 106 of 3,000 random streams with one of our orders resting at a time; now none.
Size-up build: (a) ignored our own growth. One of our orders growing in place was not re-checked for ours behind it.
prefetch(sym) did nothing. g++ treats a function that only prefetches as free of side effects and deletes any call it did not inline. Every call site I tried compiled to nothing.

The first three have regression tests that fail on the delivered headers.

